# Lombok configuration for the three new services. It lives in services/ and not at the repo root
# on purpose: bubbling from the root would also cover anything else that ever sits beside them, and
# this policy is about the services' own code. It began as a fence around the legacy monolith, which
# used @Data everywhere and had nothing to gain from a change of policy; the monolith went in v0.7
# and keeping the scope narrow is still the right default.
#
# addLombokGeneratedAnnotation is what makes the second rule of docs/03-analisis-y-patrones.md
# §3 ("ninguna @Entity está anotada con @Data") enforceable at all: lombok.Data has SOURCE
# retention, so ArchUnit can never see it in bytecode. @lombok.Generated has CLASS retention and
# is stamped on every generated method, which turns the rule into one about the equals/hashCode/
# toString an entity must write by hand. Jacoco also excludes @lombok.Generated code from its
# reports, which is a welcome side effect rather than the reason.
config.stopBubbling = true
lombok.addLombokGeneratedAnnotation = true
